{"id":"h098","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The SI base unit of luminous intensity is the lumen.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The lumen is the SI unit most closely tied to light output.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.3,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-3.1091},{"text":"The lumen is a photometric unit.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-3.1128},{"text":"The claim seems plausible because lumens and luminous intensity are often discussed together.","confidence":0.5,"lean":0.3,"theta":0.7854,"phi":0.0442},{"text":"People use 'lumen' loosely for brightness.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.2,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-1.3784},{"text":"The SI has seven base units: metre, kilogram, second, ampere, kelvin, mole, and candela.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1063},{"text":"The candela is the SI base unit for luminous intensity.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1075},{"text":"The lumen is a derived unit, 1 lm = 1 cd·sr.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1113},{"text":"The lumen measures luminous flux, the total perceived light power emitted.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1185},{"text":"Luminous intensity is measured in candelas and flux in lumens.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1115},{"text":"The claim that the lumen is the base unit of luminous intensity is false.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.0712}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":9,"J":-0.7,"relatio